# Code Conventions

## Components

- Functional components + hooks ONLY (no class components)
- Props interface: `{ComponentName}Props`
- Named exports only (no default exports)
- Colocated tests: `ComponentName.test.tsx`

## TypeScript

- Strict mode — no `any`, no `@ts-ignore`
- Prefer `type` over `interface` for simple types
- Import types: `import type { X } from "..."`

## Files

- kebab-case for files: `element-utils.ts`
- PascalCase for components: `LayerUI.tsx`

## How to Verify

1. Confirm components are function-based with hooks and no class components were introduced.
2. Confirm component props use the `{ComponentName}Props` naming convention.
3. Confirm exports are named exports only and no default exports were added.
4. Confirm tests are colocated using the `ComponentName.test.tsx` pattern where applicable.
5. Confirm TypeScript stays strict (`no any`, `no @ts-ignore`) and type-only imports use `import type`.
6. Confirm file names follow conventions: kebab-case for utility files and PascalCase for component files.